    "body": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  data-cf-product picks the accent ramp and data-cf-substrate the ash ramp, both from\n  @cloudsforge/ui/tokens.css. They are on <html> and set STATICALLY here rather than by React,\n  because a page that paints before the attributes land flashes the default ember and then\n  changes colour.\n\n  `lantern` is the real registry key (ui/packages/ui/src/surfaces.ts:375-389) and it has a\n  DECLARED block at ui/packages/ui/src/tokens.css:596-602, so nothing here falls through to the\n  company default in silence. That block carries amber — and this surface then re-points the five\n  accent tokens to the ember ramp in src/styles.css, for the reason tokens.css:594-596 states\n  verbatim. Naming some other key would have been the lazy way to get ember, and it would have\n  been a lie about which surface this is.\n-->\n<html lang=\"en-GB\" data-cf-product=\"lantern\" data-cf-substrate=\"warm\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <meta name=\"colour-scheme\" content=\"dark light\" />\n    <!--\n      The build that produced this bundle. Stamped by the Dockerfile, read by src/lib/obs.ts, and\n      the reason an error report can be pinned to the deploy that introduced it. It is an identity\n      rather than a configuration: it names the artefact, it does not tell it where it is running.\n    -->\n    <meta name=\"cf-release\" content=\"estate\" />\n    <!--\n      Lantern carries `markId: null` in the registry (surfaces.ts:385), so no mark and no wordmark\n      appear anywhere in this bundle. These are the company chrome, which a separate hostname needs\n      regardless: a browser tab and a shared link inherit nothing.\n    -->\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\" href=\"/favicon-32x32.png\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"/favicon-192x192.png\" />\n    <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"/favicon-192x192.png\" />\n\n    <title>Lantern — logs &amp; errors</title>\n\n    <!-- Relative on purpose: one bundle serves localhost, preview and the apex, and this file\n         names no hostname. Crawlers resolve it against the page they fetched. An absolute URL\n         here would bake a hostname into the artefact — the same defect as build-time config. -->\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Lantern\" />\n    <meta\n      property=\"og:description\"\n      content=\"The CloudsForge operator console for issues, events and browser samples.\"\n    />\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"/og-1200x630.png\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n    <!-- An operator console has nothing a search engine should hold. `adminOnly: true`\n         (surfaces.ts:388) is the authorisation fact; this is the indexing one, and they are not\n         the same statement. -->\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\" />\n    <script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"/assets/index-yfz3XsWJ.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/index-BaoSTAtD.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
